# Host canonicalization (4.19.2): the apex was serving the full site as a
# second origin — duplicate pages in Search Console and an independent
# service worker/cache that could wedge separately from www (the 2026-08-17
# stuck-shell incident was on the apex). Full-URL sources are the
# Pages-native way to redirect across hosts; the functions/_middleware.ts
# 301 only fires on function-backed routes, this line covers the static
# ones too. Must stay FIRST: rules match top-down.
https://sirimillavinay.online/* https://www.sirimillavinay.online/:splat 301

# Hashed build assets must NEVER fall back to the SPA shell: an HTML body
# cached under the /assets/* immutable header bricks that chunk URL for up to
# a year. A missing asset is a plain 404 — the app reloads and recovers.
/assets/*  /assets-404.txt  404

# Route aliases — legacy/guessable paths land on the real pages.
/downloads  /offline  301
/listen-together  /together  301

/*    /index.html   200
